Capture key frames from a composition as PNG screenshots for visual verification (hyperframes snapshot v0.9.59)

USAGE hyperframes snapshot [OPTIONS] [DIR]

ARGUMENTS

  DIR    Project directory

OPTIONS

  -o, -out, -output-dir, --output=<output>    Directory to write snapshots into (default: unique directory under <project>/.hyperframes/artifacts/snapshots)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
                         --frames=<frames>    Number of evenly-spaced frames to capture (Default: 5)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         
                                 --at=<at>    Comma-separated timestamps in seconds (e.g., --at 3.0,10.5,18.0). Each is captured at that exact instant, not snapped to a frame.                                                                                                                                                                                                              
                           --range=<range>    Root-timeline range START,END in seconds; sample --frames evenly within it, without adding the full-video tail                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 
               --composition=<composition>    data-composition-id to sample; take --frames within its effective root-timeline interval, without adding the full-video tail                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
                       --timeout=<timeout>    Ms to wait for the composition to become render-ready, and for each still's seek to settle, up to 170 s (Default: 45000)                                                                                                                                                                                                                       
                           --angle=<angle>    Orthogonal 3D camera for depth/occlusion checks: a preset (front|iso|top|side) or 'yaw,pitch' degrees. Tilts the whole stage before screenshotting (real pixels, not bbox markers).                                                                                                                                                            
                                     --end    Always include a readable end-of-timeline frame. Pass --no-end to capture only your exact --at times. (Default: true)                                                                                                                                                                                                                          
                                  --no-end                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   
                                    --keep    Add to --output instead of clearing it, naming each still at-<seconds>s.png (at-0s, at-1.5s, at-12.25s: no trailing zeros), so snapshotting one moment again replaces only that still. Times less than 1 ms apart share a name, so one run may not pass two of them. No contact sheet. (Default: false)                                        
                             --zoom=<zoom>    Zoom into a CSS selector or an exact pixel region 'x,y,w,h'. Crops a high-density screenshot instead of the full frame — a raised deviceScaleFactor, never CSS zoom or viewport resizing, so layout stays identical. A selector matching nothing is an error, not a silent full-frame shot.                                                    
                 --zoom-scale=<zoom_scale>    Device-scale-factor density for --zoom crops (Default: 3)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
                       --against=<against>    Reference video (e.g. footage being rebuilt): also save its frame at each captured time and a render|reference pair sheet                                                                                                                                                                                                                      
                                  --review    Capture the review set instead of evenly spaced frames: each scene at its start + 0.3 s and its middle, and each data-beat at its start + 0.3 s, on review-beats.jpg, a 5-frame strip around every cut (review-seam-NN.jpg), and the beat frames at phone width (review-phone.jpg). Scopes to --composition; ignores --frames. (Default: false)
                                    --json    Print one JSON envelope (paths, times, sheets; the review plan under --review) (Default: false)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                
                     --describe=<describe>    Send each frame to Gemini for a vision description (off by default; needs GEMINI_API_KEY or GOOGLE_API_KEY). A bare --describe uses the default prompt; --describe 'Is the logo visible in every beat?' asks your own question.                                                                                                                
                                   --proxy    Serve browser-playable copies of hostile video codecs to the snapshot page (default: off; frames come from FFmpeg, and each copy transcodes the whole clip)                                                                                                                                                                                    
                             --browser-gpu    Use hardware browser GPU capture; pass --no-browser-gpu for deterministic SwiftShader (default: auto-detect, PRODUCER_BROWSER_GPU_MODE overrides)                                                                                                                                                                                              


Use only one of --at, --range, or --composition
